The predefined CMaps a Type0 font's /Encoding names (ISO 32000-1 Table 118)
and Adobe-CNS1-UCS2, Adobe-GB1-UCS2, Adobe-Japan1-UCS2 and Adobe-Korea1-UCS2
are Adobe's (https://github.com/adobe-type-tools/cmap-resources), as the
hayro-cmap crate bundles them (https://github.com/LaurenzV/hayro, the crate
Apache-2.0 OR MIT; its assets/cmaps.brotli and assets/LICENSE.txt). sheaf
reads each code's CID with them, and a CID's text where a font has no
/ToUnicode. They are distributed under the BSD 3-Clause license; the bundle's
notice, assets/LICENSE.txt, follows unmodified.

